 {
  "id": "system-design-loop",
  "after": "outcomes",
  "title": "A system design answer, step by step.",
  "caption": "Here the product is a support bot for a D2C (direct-to-consumer) kurta brand, one that sells straight to buyers online. Answer the seven parts in this order, with a number wherever you can. Steps 1 to 4 happen before launch; steps 5 to 7 keep it running. The cost is a simple sum: the LLM (the AI model that writes the replies) costs 30,000 chats × ₹0.25 = ₹7,500, and the server about ₹2,500 more. The red arrow is the part beginners forget: monitoring (निगरानी, nigrani) finds questions the bot gets wrong, and you fix the data so the next version answers them.",
  "alt": "A numbered column of seven boxes for a support bot of a D2C kurta brand. 1 requirements: Hindi and English, reply in under 3 seconds. 2 data: FAQs, return policy and live order data. 3 model: RAG, which fetches the right documents before an LLM replies. 4 evaluation: 200 past questions, aiming for 90 percent right. Then a \"go live\" line. 5 serving: WhatsApp and website chat through a cloud API. 6 monitoring: log wrong answers and chats handed to staff. 7 cost: about 10,000 rupees a month for 30,000 chats. A red arrow loops from monitoring back to data, labelled improve.",
  "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 360 446\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><rect x=\"12\" y=\"10\" width=\"336\" height=\"34\" rx=\"12\" class=\"f-surface2 s-line\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"180\" y=\"32\" font-size=\"14\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><tspan font-weight=\"700\">Design:</tspan> support bot for a D2C kurta brand</text><rect x=\"46\" y=\"56\" width=\"268\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" class=\"f-indigo-soft s-indigo\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><text x=\"58\" y=\"74\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"700\">Requirements</text><text x=\"58\" y=\"92\" font-size=\"13\">Hindi + English; reply in under 3 s</text><rect x=\"46\" y=\"108\" width=\"268\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" class=\"f-indigo-soft s-indigo\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><text x=\"58\" y=\"126\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"700\">Data</text><text x=\"58\" y=\"144\" font-size=\"13\">FAQs, return policy, live order data</text><rect x=\"46\" y=\"160\" width=\"268\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" class=\"f-indigo-soft s-indigo\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><text x=\"58\" y=\"178\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"700\">Model</text><text x=\"58\" y=\"196\" font-size=\"13\">RAG: fetch the right docs, LLM replies</text><rect x=\"46\" y=\"212\" width=\"268\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" class=\"f-indigo-soft s-indigo\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><text x=\"58\" y=\"230\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"700\">Evaluation</text><text x=\"58\" y=\"248\" font-size=\"13\">200 past questions; aim for 90% right</text><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"273\" x2=\"348\" y2=\"273\" class=\"s-muted\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke-dasharray=\"5 4\"/><rect x=\"140\" y=\"262\" width=\"80\" height=\"22\" rx=\"11\" class=\"f-surface\"/><text x=\"180\" y=\"278\" font-size=\"13\" class=\"f-muted\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\">go live</text><rect x=\"46\" y=\"286\" width=\"268\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" class=\"f-haldi-soft s-haldi\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><text x=\"58\" y=\"304\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"700\">Serving</text><text x=\"58\" y=\"322\" font-size=\"13\">WhatsApp + website chat, cloud API</text><rect x=\"46\" y=\"338\" width=\"268\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" class=\"f-haldi-soft s-haldi\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><text x=\"58\" y=\"356\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"700\">Monitoring</text><text x=\"58\" y=\"374\" font-size=\"13\">Log wrong answers, hand-offs to staff</text><rect x=\"46\" y=\"390\" width=\"268\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" class=\"f-haldi-soft s-haldi\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><text x=\"58\" y=\"408\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"700\">Cost</text><text x=\"58\" y=\"426\" font-size=\"13\">≈ ₹10,000 a month for 30,000 chats</text><line x1=\"24\" y1=\"89\" x2=\"24\" y2=\"119\" class=\"s-line\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"24\" cy=\"78\" r=\"11\" class=\"f-indigo-soft s-indigo\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"24\" y=\"82.6\" font-size=\"13\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\">1</text><line x1=\"24\" y1=\"141\" x2=\"24\" y2=\"171\" class=\"s-line\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"24\" cy=\"130\" r=\"11\" class=\"f-indigo-soft s-indigo\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"24\" y=\"134.6\" font-size=\"13\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\">2</text><line x1=\"24\" y1=\"193\" x2=\"24\" y2=\"223\" class=\"s-line\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"24\" cy=\"182\" r=\"11\" class=\"f-indigo-soft s-indigo\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"24\" y=\"186.6\" font-size=\"13\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\">3</text><line x1=\"24\" y1=\"245\" x2=\"24\" y2=\"297\" class=\"s-line\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"24\" cy=\"234\" r=\"11\" class=\"f-indigo-soft s-indigo\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"24\" y=\"238.6\" font-size=\"13\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\">4</text><line x1=\"24\" y1=\"319\" x2=\"24\" y2=\"349\" class=\"s-line\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"24\" cy=\"308\" r=\"11\" class=\"f-haldi-soft s-haldi\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"24\" y=\"312.6\" font-size=\"13\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\">5</text><line x1=\"24\" y1=\"371\" x2=\"24\" y2=\"401\" class=\"s-line\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"24\" cy=\"360\" r=\"11\" class=\"f-haldi-soft s-haldi\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"24\" y=\"364.6\" font-size=\"13\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\">6</text><circle cx=\"24\" cy=\"412\" r=\"11\" class=\"f-haldi-soft s-haldi\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"24\" y=\"416.6\" font-size=\"13\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\">7</text><path d=\"M314 360.0 H330 V130.0 H322\" class=\"f-none s-sindoor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><polygon points=\"315,130 323,125.6 323,134.4\" class=\"f-sindoor\"/><text x=\"0\" y=\"0\" font-size=\"13\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"f-muted\" font-weight=\"700\" transform=\"translate(346 197.5) rotate(-90)\">improve</text></svg>"
 },
 {
  "id": "traffic-sum",
  "after": "outcomes",
  "title": "A back-of-the-envelope traffic sum.",
  "caption": "Interviewers often ask for a quick estimate (अंदाज़ा, andaaza) like this. It is called back-of-the-envelope because it is small enough to work out on the back of an envelope. A day has 86,400 seconds, so 5 crore requests a day is about 579 a second on average. In Python, `50_00_000 * 10 / 86_400` gives 578.7; the underscores only make big numbers easy to read. Traffic is not even: if the busiest hour has 3 times the average, you need about 1,736 a second, so plan servers for that peak.",
  "alt": "A worked sum. 50 lakh users times 10 requests a day equals 5 crore requests a day. Divided by 86,400 seconds in a day, that is about 579 requests a second. Times 3 in the busiest hour, about 1,736 a second. A grey box shows the same sum as one line of Python, 50_00_000 times 10 divided by 86_400, which gives 578.7. A bar chart starting at zero shows the average bar of 579 and a peak bar three times longer at 1,736. A green box says to plan servers for the peak, not the average. A red note warns that dividing by 1,440 minutes gives 34,722, which is per minute, not per second.",
  "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 360 434\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><rect x=\"12\" y=\"10\" width=\"336\" height=\"34\" rx=\"12\" class=\"f-surface2 s-line\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"180\" y=\"32\" font-size=\"14\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\">50 lakh users × 10 requests a day</text><rect x=\"12\" y=\"56\" width=\"336\" height=\"36\" rx=\"8\" class=\"f-indigo-soft s-indigo\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><text x=\"24\" y=\"79\" font-size=\"14\">= 5 crore requests a day</text><rect x=\"12\" y=\"100\" width=\"336\" height=\"36\" rx=\"8\" class=\"f-indigo-soft s-indigo\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><text x=\"24\" y=\"123\" font-size=\"14\">÷ 86,400 seconds in a day</text><text x=\"336\" y=\"123\" font-size=\"14\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-weight=\"700\">≈ 579 a second</text><rect x=\"12\" y=\"144\" width=\"336\" height=\"36\" rx=\"8\" class=\"f-haldi-soft s-haldi\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><text x=\"24\" y=\"167\" font-size=\"14\">× 3 in the busiest hour</text><text x=\"336\" y=\"167\" font-size=\"14\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-weight=\"700\">≈ 1,736 a second</text><rect x=\"12\" y=\"188\" width=\"336\" height=\"32\" rx=\"8\" class=\"f-surface2 s-line\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><text x=\"24\" y=\"209\" font-size=\"13\" class=\"f-muted\" font-weight=\"700\">Python:</text><text x=\"84\" y=\"209\" font-size=\"13\" class=\"mono\" style=\"font-size:13px\">50_00_000 * 10 / 86_400</text><text x=\"336\" y=\"209\" font-size=\"13\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-weight=\"700\">→ 578.7</text><text x=\"12\" y=\"242\" font-size=\"13\" class=\"f-muted\" font-weight=\"700\">Requests per second (bars start at 0)</text><text x=\"76\" y=\"273\" font-size=\"14\" text-anchor=\"end\">Average</text><rect x=\"84\" y=\"258\" width=\"80\" height=\"22\" rx=\"3\" class=\"f-indigo\"/><text x=\"156\" y=\"274\" font-size=\"13\" class=\"f-bg\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-weight=\"700\">579</text><text x=\"76\" y=\"305\" font-size=\"14\" text-anchor=\"end\">Peak</text><rect x=\"84\" y=\"290\" width=\"240\" height=\"22\" rx=\"3\" class=\"f-haldi\"/><text x=\"316\" y=\"306\" font-size=\"13\" class=\"f-bg\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-weight=\"700\">1,736</text><line x1=\"84\" y1=\"248\" x2=\"84\" y2=\"316\" class=\"s-muted\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><rect x=\"12\" y=\"332\" width=\"336\" height=\"50\" rx=\"8\" class=\"f-ok-soft s-ok\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><text x=\"24\" y=\"351\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"700\">Plan servers for the peak, not</text><text x=\"24\" y=\"370\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"700\">the average: about 1,736 a second.</text><text x=\"12\" y=\"406\" font-size=\"13\" class=\"f-bad\">Slip to avoid: ÷ 1,440 minutes gives 34,722.</text><text x=\"12\" y=\"424\" font-size=\"13\" class=\"f-bad\">That is per minute, not per second.</text></svg>"
 },
 {
  "id": "reproduce-check",
  "after": "studySteps",
  "title": "Reproducing a result, step by step.",
  "caption": "First run the paper's released code on a small slice of the data and compare with its table. If your number differs, look for hidden details in the appendix and official code. Then run several seeds: if the paper's number falls inside the range of your runs, the result reproduces. The numbers are made up.",
  "alt": "Four numbered steps. 1: run the paper's code on a small slice of the data in Colab. 2: compare with its table: paper 81.0, yours 80.4. 3: if there is a gap, check the appendix and official code for the data split, cleaning steps, settings and scoring. 4: run 5 seeds, where a seed is the random start of training; a dot strip shows five runs at 80.4, 80.5, 80.8, 81.1 and 81.2, and a red line marks the paper's 81.0 inside that range. A green box says the result reproduces. A red box says that for a big gap you cannot explain, you dig deeper or politely ask the authors.",
  "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 360 414\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><rect x=\"46\" y=\"10\" width=\"302\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" class=\"f-indigo-soft s-indigo\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><text x=\"58\" y=\"28\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"700\">Run the paper’s code</text><text x=\"58\" y=\"46\" font-size=\"13\">small slice of the data, in Colab</text><rect x=\"46\" y=\"64\" width=\"302\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" class=\"f-indigo-soft s-indigo\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><text x=\"58\" y=\"82\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"700\">Compare with its table</text><text x=\"58\" y=\"100\" font-size=\"13\">paper 81.0  ·  yours 80.4</text><rect x=\"46\" y=\"118\" width=\"302\" height=\"60\" rx=\"8\" class=\"f-indigo-soft s-indigo\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><text x=\"58\" y=\"136\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"700\">Gap? Check the details</text><text x=\"58\" y=\"154\" font-size=\"13\">appendix + official code: data split,</text><text x=\"58\" y=\"171\" font-size=\"13\">cleaning steps, settings, scoring</text><rect x=\"46\" y=\"188\" width=\"302\" height=\"106\" rx=\"8\" class=\"f-indigo-soft s-indigo\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><text x=\"58\" y=\"206\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"700\">Run 5 seeds</text><text x=\"58\" y=\"224\" font-size=\"13\">seed = the random start of training</text><line x1=\"70\" y1=\"270\" x2=\"330\" y2=\"270\" class=\"s-muted\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><line x1=\"70\" y1=\"270\" x2=\"70\" y2=\"274\" class=\"s-muted\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><text x=\"70\" y=\"288\" font-size=\"13\" class=\"f-muted\" text-anchor=\"middle\">80.0</text><line x1=\"156.7\" y1=\"270\" x2=\"156.7\" y2=\"274\" class=\"s-muted\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><text x=\"156.7\" y=\"288\" font-size=\"13\" class=\"f-muted\" text-anchor=\"middle\">80.5</text><line x1=\"243.3\" y1=\"270\" x2=\"243.3\" y2=\"274\" class=\"s-muted\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><text x=\"243.3\" y=\"288\" font-size=\"13\" class=\"f-muted\" text-anchor=\"middle\">81.0</text><line x1=\"330\" y1=\"270\" x2=\"330\" y2=\"274\" class=\"s-muted\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><text x=\"330\" y=\"288\" font-size=\"13\" class=\"f-muted\" text-anchor=\"middle\">81.5</text><rect x=\"139.3\" y=\"252\" width=\"138.7\" height=\"12\" rx=\"3\" class=\"f-ok-soft\"/><circle cx=\"139.3\" cy=\"258\" r=\"4.5\" class=\"f-indigo\"/><circle cx=\"156.7\" cy=\"258\" r=\"4.5\" class=\"f-indigo\"/><circle cx=\"208.7\" cy=\"258\" r=\"4.5\" class=\"f-indigo\"/><circle cx=\"260.7\" cy=\"258\" r=\"4.5\" class=\"f-indigo\"/><circle cx=\"278\" cy=\"258\" r=\"4.5\" class=\"f-indigo\"/><line x1=\"243.3\" y1=\"234\" x2=\"243.3\" y2=\"268\" class=\"s-sindoor\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"249.3\" y=\"244\" font-size=\"13\" class=\"f-sindoor\" font-weight=\"700\">paper</text><line x1=\"24\" y1=\"43\" x2=\"24\" y2=\"75\" class=\"s-line\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"24\" cy=\"32\" r=\"11\" class=\"f-indigo-soft s-indigo\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"24\" y=\"36.6\" font-size=\"13\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\">1</text><line x1=\"24\" y1=\"97\" x2=\"24\" y2=\"129\" class=\"s-line\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"24\" cy=\"86\" r=\"11\" class=\"f-indigo-soft s-indigo\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"24\" y=\"90.6\" font-size=\"13\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\">2</text><line x1=\"24\" y1=\"151\" x2=\"24\" y2=\"199\" class=\"s-line\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"24\" cy=\"140\" r=\"11\" class=\"f-indigo-soft s-indigo\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"24\" y=\"144.6\" font-size=\"13\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\">3</text><circle cx=\"24\" cy=\"210\" r=\"11\" class=\"f-indigo-soft s-indigo\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"24\" y=\"214.6\" font-size=\"13\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\">4</text><rect x=\"12\" y=\"304\" width=\"336\" height=\"46\" rx=\"8\" class=\"f-ok-soft s-ok\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><text x=\"24\" y=\"323\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"700\">Paper’s 81.0 is inside your range</text><text x=\"24\" y=\"341\" font-size=\"13\">80.4 to 81.2, so the result reproduces.</text><rect x=\"12\" y=\"358\" width=\"336\" height=\"46\" rx=\"8\" class=\"f-bad-soft s-bad\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><text x=\"24\" y=\"377\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"700\">Big gap you cannot explain?</text><text x=\"24\" y=\"395\" font-size=\"13\">Dig deeper, or ask the authors politely.</text></svg>"
 },
 {
  "id": "ablation-table",
  "after": "keyTerms",
  "title": "An ablation study and a baseline in one chart.",
  "caption": "An ablation study removes one part at a time. Removing part B drops accuracy by 3.5 points, so B does most of the work; parts A and C add little. The baseline (the old method) shows how much the whole new model gains. The paper is made up, and the bars start at 75 to make small gaps visible.",
  "alt": "A horizontal bar chart of accuracy for a made-up Hindi spam filter, with the axis from 75 to 83. Full model with parts A, B and C: 82.0. Without part A: 81.8, minus 0.2. Without part B: 78.5, minus 3.5, shown in red. Without part C: 81.6, minus 0.4. Below a dashed line, the baseline or old method: 77.0. A note explains that an ablation removes one part at a time, that B matters most and A adds almost nothing, and that the baseline is the old method to beat.",
  "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 360 332\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><text x=\"12\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"700\">Made-up paper: a Hindi spam filter</text><text x=\"12\" y=\"40\" font-size=\"13\" class=\"f-muted\">Accuracy in % (bars start at 75, not 0)</text><text x=\"12\" y=\"73\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"700\">Full model (A+B+C)</text><rect x=\"150\" y=\"60\" width=\"122.5\" height=\"20\" rx=\"3\" class=\"f-indigo\"/><text x=\"278.5\" y=\"75\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\">82.0</text><text x=\"12\" y=\"105\" font-size=\"14\">Without part A</text><rect x=\"150\" y=\"92\" width=\"119\" height=\"20\" rx=\"3\" class=\"f-s1\"/><text x=\"275\" y=\"107\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\">81.8</text><text x=\"348\" y=\"107\" font-size=\"13\" class=\"f-muted\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-weight=\"700\">−0.2</text><text x=\"12\" y=\"137\" font-size=\"14\">Without part B</text><rect x=\"150\" y=\"124\" width=\"61.2\" height=\"20\" rx=\"3\" class=\"f-bad\"/><text x=\"217.2\" y=\"139\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\">78.5</text><text x=\"348\" y=\"139\" font-size=\"13\" class=\"f-bad\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-weight=\"700\">−3.5</text><text x=\"12\" y=\"169\" font-size=\"14\">Without part C</text><rect x=\"150\" y=\"156\" width=\"115.5\" height=\"20\" rx=\"3\" class=\"f-s1\"/><text x=\"271.5\" y=\"171\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\">81.6</text><text x=\"348\" y=\"171\" font-size=\"13\" class=\"f-muted\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-weight=\"700\">−0.4</text><line x1=\"12\" y1=\"180\" x2=\"348\" y2=\"180\" class=\"s-line\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"/><text x=\"12\" y=\"207\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"700\">Baseline (old way)</text><rect x=\"150\" y=\"194\" width=\"35\" height=\"20\" rx=\"3\" class=\"f-muted\"/><text x=\"191\" y=\"209\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\">77.0</text><line x1=\"150\" y1=\"224\" x2=\"290\" y2=\"224\" class=\"s-muted\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><line x1=\"150\" y1=\"224\" x2=\"150\" y2=\"228\" class=\"s-muted\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><text x=\"150\" y=\"242\" font-size=\"13\" class=\"f-muted\" text-anchor=\"middle\">75</text><line x1=\"220\" y1=\"224\" x2=\"220\" y2=\"228\" class=\"s-muted\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><text x=\"220\" y=\"242\" font-size=\"13\" class=\"f-muted\" text-anchor=\"middle\">79</text><line x1=\"290\" y1=\"224\" x2=\"290\" y2=\"228\" class=\"s-muted\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><text x=\"290\" y=\"242\" font-size=\"13\" class=\"f-muted\" text-anchor=\"middle\">83</text><rect x=\"12\" y=\"258\" width=\"336\" height=\"64\" rx=\"8\" class=\"f-surface2 s-line\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"24\" y=\"278\" font-size=\"13\"><tspan font-weight=\"700\">Ablation:</tspan> remove one part at a time.</text><text x=\"24\" y=\"296\" font-size=\"13\">B matters most; A adds almost nothing.</text><text x=\"24\" y=\"314\" font-size=\"13\"><tspan font-weight=\"700\">Baseline:</tspan> the old method to beat.</text></svg>"
 },
 {
  "id": "two-stage-recommender",
  "after": "keyTerms",
  "title": "ML system design: two stages beat one slow model.",
  "caption": "A shopping app cannot score 10 crore products with a heavy model for every user in 200 milliseconds. So stage 1 uses a fast, rough search to pick about 500 likely products (candidates). Stage 2 runs the heavy, accurate model on only those 500. The latency (देरी, deri) bar shows how the 200 ms might be shared. All times are example numbers.",
  "alt": "A funnel. 10 crore products go through stage 1, a fast search of about 30 milliseconds using similar items, popular items and recent views, which leaves about 500 candidates. Stage 2, a heavy model of about 120 milliseconds, scores only these 500, and the top 10 are shown. Below, a latency budget bar of 200 milliseconds is split into search 30, ranking 120, and network and the rest 50. A red note says scoring all 10 crore products with the heavy model would take far longer than 200 milliseconds. Boxes are not to scale.",
  "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 360 382\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><text x=\"12\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"700\">Show 10 picks in under 200 ms</text><text x=\"12\" y=\"40\" font-size=\"13\" class=\"f-muted\">Example numbers; boxes not to scale</text><rect x=\"12\" y=\"52\" width=\"336\" height=\"34\" rx=\"8\" class=\"f-surface2 s-line\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><text x=\"26\" y=\"74\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"700\">10 crore products</text><line x1=\"30\" y1=\"88\" x2=\"30\" y2=\"123\" class=\"s-muted\" stroke-width=\"1.8\"/><polygon points=\"30,130 25.6,122 34.4,122\" class=\"f-muted\"/><text x=\"46\" y=\"106\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\">Stage 1: fast search, about 30 ms</text><text x=\"46\" y=\"123\" font-size=\"13\" class=\"f-muted\">similar items, popular, recent</text><rect x=\"12\" y=\"132\" width=\"236\" height=\"34\" rx=\"8\" class=\"f-indigo-soft s-indigo\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><text x=\"26\" y=\"154\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"700\">about 500 candidates</text><line x1=\"30\" y1=\"168\" x2=\"30\" y2=\"203\" class=\"s-muted\" stroke-width=\"1.8\"/><polygon points=\"30,210 25.6,202 34.4,202\" class=\"f-muted\"/><text x=\"46\" y=\"186\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\">Stage 2: heavy model, about 120 ms</text><text x=\"46\" y=\"203\" font-size=\"13\" class=\"f-muted\">scores only these 500</text><rect x=\"12\" y=\"212\" width=\"150\" height=\"34\" rx=\"8\" class=\"f-ok-soft s-ok\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><text x=\"26\" y=\"234\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"700\">Top 10 shown</text><text x=\"12\" y=\"276\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"700\">Latency budget: 200 ms in all</text><rect x=\"12\" y=\"286\" width=\"50.4\" height=\"24\" class=\"f-indigo s-line\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"12\" y=\"328\" font-size=\"13\" text-anchor=\"start\">search 30</text><rect x=\"62.4\" y=\"286\" width=\"201.6\" height=\"24\" class=\"f-haldi s-line\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"163.2\" y=\"328\" font-size=\"13\" text-anchor=\"middle\">ranking 120</text><rect x=\"264\" y=\"286\" width=\"84\" height=\"24\" class=\"f-surface2 s-line\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"348\" y=\"328\" font-size=\"13\" text-anchor=\"end\">network, rest 50</text><text x=\"12\" y=\"354\" font-size=\"13\" class=\"f-bad\">Scoring all 10 crore with the heavy model</text><text x=\"12\" y=\"372\" font-size=\"13\" class=\"f-bad\">would take far longer than 200 ms.</text></svg>"
 },
 {
  "id": "indictrans2-kit",
  "after": "indiaExample",
  "title": "IndicTrans2: everything you need to reproduce it.",
  "caption": "AI4Bharat released the data, models, test sets, code and a Colab notebook with the paper. So you can translate a slice of the IN22 test sets yourself and put your score next to the paper's. The same model also helped build AI4Bharat's Hindi model Airavata, by translating (अनुवाद, anuvaad) English training data.",
  "alt": "At the top, the IndicTrans2 paper from 2023, by AI4Bharat at IIT Madras, arXiv 2305.16307. Below, six ticked boxes list what was released with it: BPCC training data, trained models, IN22 test sets, training code, inference code and a Colab notebook. Then four numbered steps for your reproduction: open the Colab notebook, translate a slice of IN22, score it next to the paper's score, and explain any gap honestly. A green box at the bottom notes that AI4Bharat reused the model to translate English training data into Hindi for its Airavata model.",
  "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 360 416\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><rect x=\"12\" y=\"10\" width=\"336\" height=\"50\" rx=\"10\" class=\"f-surface2 s-line\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"180\" y=\"31\" font-size=\"15\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\">IndicTrans2 paper (2023)</text><text x=\"180\" y=\"50\" font-size=\"13\" class=\"f-muted\" text-anchor=\"middle\">AI4Bharat, IIT Madras · arXiv 2305.16307</text><text x=\"12\" y=\"84\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"700\">Released with the paper</text><rect x=\"12\" y=\"94\" width=\"166\" height=\"26\" rx=\"6\" class=\"f-indigo-soft s-indigo\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><path d=\"M22 107 l4 4 l7 -8\" class=\"f-none s-ok\" stroke-width=\"2.2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><text x=\"40\" y=\"112\" font-size=\"13\">BPCC training data</text><rect x=\"182\" y=\"94\" width=\"166\" height=\"26\" rx=\"6\" class=\"f-indigo-soft s-indigo\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><path d=\"M192 107 l4 4 l7 -8\" class=\"f-none s-ok\" stroke-width=\"2.2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><text x=\"210\" y=\"112\" font-size=\"13\">Trained models</text><rect x=\"12\" y=\"126\" width=\"166\" height=\"26\" rx=\"6\" class=\"f-indigo-soft s-indigo\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><path d=\"M22 139 l4 4 l7 -8\" class=\"f-none s-ok\" stroke-width=\"2.2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><text x=\"40\" y=\"144\" font-size=\"13\">IN22 test sets</text><rect x=\"182\" y=\"126\" width=\"166\" height=\"26\" rx=\"6\" class=\"f-indigo-soft s-indigo\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><path d=\"M192 139 l4 4 l7 -8\" class=\"f-none s-ok\" stroke-width=\"2.2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><text x=\"210\" y=\"144\" font-size=\"13\">Training code</text><rect x=\"12\" y=\"158\" width=\"166\" height=\"26\" rx=\"6\" class=\"f-indigo-soft s-indigo\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><path d=\"M22 171 l4 4 l7 -8\" class=\"f-none s-ok\" stroke-width=\"2.2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><text x=\"40\" y=\"176\" font-size=\"13\">Inference code</text><rect x=\"182\" y=\"158\" width=\"166\" height=\"26\" rx=\"6\" class=\"f-indigo-soft s-indigo\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><path d=\"M192 171 l4 4 l7 -8\" class=\"f-none s-ok\" stroke-width=\"2.2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><text x=\"210\" y=\"176\" font-size=\"13\">Colab notebook</text><text x=\"12\" y=\"208\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"700\">Your reproduction</text><rect x=\"46\" y=\"218\" width=\"302\" height=\"28\" rx=\"6\" class=\"f-haldi-soft s-haldi\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><circle cx=\"24\" cy=\"232\" r=\"10\" class=\"f-haldi-soft s-haldi\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"24\" y=\"236.6\" font-size=\"13\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\">1</text><text x=\"58\" y=\"237\" font-size=\"13\">Open the Colab notebook</text><line x1=\"24\" y1=\"242\" x2=\"24\" y2=\"252\" class=\"s-line\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><rect x=\"46\" y=\"252\" width=\"302\" height=\"28\" rx=\"6\" class=\"f-haldi-soft s-haldi\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><circle cx=\"24\" cy=\"266\" r=\"10\" class=\"f-haldi-soft s-haldi\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"24\" y=\"270.6\" font-size=\"13\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\">2</text><text x=\"58\" y=\"271\" font-size=\"13\">Translate a slice of IN22</text><line x1=\"24\" y1=\"276\" x2=\"24\" y2=\"286\" class=\"s-line\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><rect x=\"46\" y=\"286\" width=\"302\" height=\"28\" rx=\"6\" class=\"f-haldi-soft s-haldi\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><circle cx=\"24\" cy=\"300\" r=\"10\" class=\"f-haldi-soft s-haldi\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"24\" y=\"304.6\" font-size=\"13\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\">3</text><text x=\"58\" y=\"305\" font-size=\"13\">Score it, next to the paper’s score</text><line x1=\"24\" y1=\"310\" x2=\"24\" y2=\"320\" class=\"s-line\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><rect x=\"46\" y=\"320\" width=\"302\" height=\"28\" rx=\"6\" class=\"f-haldi-soft s-haldi\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><circle cx=\"24\" cy=\"334\" r=\"10\" class=\"f-haldi-soft s-haldi\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"24\" y=\"338.6\" font-size=\"13\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\">4</text><text x=\"58\" y=\"339\" font-size=\"13\">Explain any gap honestly</text><rect x=\"12\" y=\"360\" width=\"336\" height=\"46\" rx=\"8\" class=\"f-ok-soft s-ok\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><text x=\"24\" y=\"379\" font-size=\"13\"><tspan font-weight=\"700\">Reused:</tspan> AI4Bharat translated English</text><text x=\"24\" y=\"397\" font-size=\"13\">training data into Hindi with it for Airavata.</text></svg>"
 },
 {
  "id": "seed-luck",
  "after": "commonMistakes",
  "title": "One lucky seed is not proof.",
  "caption": "Each dot is one training run with a different seed (the random start of training). \"80.8 ± 0.4\" means the mean (average) is 80.8 and runs usually land within about 0.4 of it. The new method's mean is only 0.3 higher, which is smaller than the usual spread (फैलाव, phailaav) between runs, so it may be luck. Showing only the best seed makes it look like +1.1; that is cherry-picking. In NumPy, `scores.mean()` and `scores.std()` give these two numbers. The runs are made up.",
  "alt": "A dot plot with the axis from 80 to 82. The baseline row has five dots at 80.2, 80.6, 80.9, 81.0 and 81.4, with mean 80.8 plus or minus 0.4. The new method row has five dots at 80.5, 80.7, 81.2, 81.3 and 81.9, with mean 81.1 plus or minus 0.5. The two ranges overlap a lot. A red box says that showing only the best seed, 81.9 against 80.8, looks like a 1.1 point win, but one seed is luck, not proof. A green box says to report the mean plus or minus the spread: the gap of 0.3 is smaller than the spread, so there is no claim yet.",
  "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 360 354\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><text x=\"12\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"700\">Accuracy over 5 seeds (made-up runs)</text><text x=\"12\" y=\"40\" font-size=\"13\" class=\"f-muted\">Axis starts at 80, not 0</text><text x=\"12\" y=\"69\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"700\">Baseline</text><line x1=\"153.6\" y1=\"64\" x2=\"248\" y2=\"64\" class=\"s-ink\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><line x1=\"153.6\" y1=\"58\" x2=\"153.6\" y2=\"70\" class=\"s-ink\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><line x1=\"248\" y1=\"58\" x2=\"248\" y2=\"70\" class=\"s-ink\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"127.6\" cy=\"64\" r=\"5\" class=\"f-muted\"/><circle cx=\"174.8\" cy=\"64\" r=\"5\" class=\"f-muted\"/><circle cx=\"210.2\" cy=\"64\" r=\"5\" class=\"f-muted\"/><circle cx=\"222\" cy=\"64\" r=\"5\" class=\"f-muted\"/><circle cx=\"269.2\" cy=\"64\" r=\"5\" class=\"f-muted\"/><line x1=\"200.8\" y1=\"54\" x2=\"200.8\" y2=\"74\" class=\"s-sindoor\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><text x=\"200.8\" y=\"92\" font-size=\"13\" text-anchor=\"middle\">mean 80.8 ± 0.4</text><text x=\"12\" y=\"131\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"700\">New method</text><line x1=\"178.3\" y1=\"126\" x2=\"294\" y2=\"126\" class=\"s-ink\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><line x1=\"178.3\" y1=\"120\" x2=\"178.3\" y2=\"132\" class=\"s-ink\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><line x1=\"294\" y1=\"120\" x2=\"294\" y2=\"132\" class=\"s-ink\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"163\" cy=\"126\" r=\"5\" class=\"f-indigo\"/><circle cx=\"186.6\" cy=\"126\" r=\"5\" class=\"f-indigo\"/><circle cx=\"245.6\" cy=\"126\" r=\"5\" class=\"f-indigo\"/><circle cx=\"257.4\" cy=\"126\" r=\"5\" class=\"f-indigo\"/><circle cx=\"328.2\" cy=\"126\" r=\"5\" class=\"f-indigo\"/><line x1=\"236.2\" y1=\"116\" x2=\"236.2\" y2=\"136\" class=\"s-sindoor\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><text x=\"236.2\" y=\"154\" font-size=\"13\" text-anchor=\"middle\">mean 81.1 ± 0.5</text><line x1=\"104\" y1=\"172\" x2=\"340\" y2=\"172\" class=\"s-muted\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><line x1=\"104\" y1=\"172\" x2=\"104\" y2=\"176\" class=\"s-muted\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><text x=\"104\" y=\"190\" font-size=\"13\" class=\"f-muted\" text-anchor=\"middle\">80.0</text><line x1=\"163\" y1=\"172\" x2=\"163\" y2=\"176\" class=\"s-muted\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><text x=\"163\" y=\"190\" font-size=\"13\" class=\"f-muted\" text-anchor=\"middle\">80.5</text><line x1=\"222\" y1=\"172\" x2=\"222\" y2=\"176\" class=\"s-muted\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><text x=\"222\" y=\"190\" font-size=\"13\" class=\"f-muted\" text-anchor=\"middle\">81.0</text><line x1=\"281\" y1=\"172\" x2=\"281\" y2=\"176\" class=\"s-muted\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><text x=\"281\" y=\"190\" font-size=\"13\" class=\"f-muted\" text-anchor=\"middle\">81.5</text><line x1=\"340\" y1=\"172\" x2=\"340\" y2=\"176\" class=\"s-muted\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><text x=\"340\" y=\"190\" font-size=\"13\" class=\"f-muted\" text-anchor=\"middle\">82.0</text><rect x=\"12\" y=\"208\" width=\"336\" height=\"64\" rx=\"8\" class=\"f-bad-soft s-bad\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><text x=\"24\" y=\"228\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\">Cherry-picked: show only the best seed</text><text x=\"24\" y=\"246\" font-size=\"13\">81.9 against 80.8 looks like a +1.1 win.</text><text x=\"24\" y=\"264\" font-size=\"13\">One seed is luck, not proof.</text><rect x=\"12\" y=\"280\" width=\"336\" height=\"64\" rx=\"8\" class=\"f-ok-soft s-ok\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><text x=\"24\" y=\"300\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\">Honest: report mean ± spread</text><text x=\"24\" y=\"318\" font-size=\"13\">Gap 0.3 is smaller than the spread</text><text x=\"24\" y=\"336\" font-size=\"13\">(0.4 to 0.5), so: no claim yet.</text></svg>"
 },
 {
  "id": "unfair-comparison",
  "after": "commonMistakes",
  "title": "An unfair comparison makes a big fake gain.",
  "caption": "In the top panel, the new model got 200 tuning tries and the baseline got one, and the settings were picked by test score. That shows a 3-point gain. In a fair (निष्पक्ष, nishpaksh) re-run, both get 200 tries on a validation set, and the test set is used once at the end. The real gain is only 0.4. The scores are made up.",
  "alt": "Two panels of bar charts, with bars starting at 80. The red \"Unfair\" panel: the new model with 200 tries scores 85.0, the baseline with 1 try and default settings scores 82.0, a gap of 3.0 points, and a note says the settings were picked by test score so the test set is no longer unseen. The green \"Fair\" panel: the new model with 200 tries scores 84.0, the baseline with 200 tries scores 83.6, a gap of 0.4 points, with both tuned on a validation set and the test set used once at the end.",
  "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 360 446\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><text x=\"12\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"13\" class=\"f-muted\">Made-up scores; bars start at 80</text><rect x=\"12\" y=\"32\" width=\"336\" height=\"196\" rx=\"10\" class=\"f-bad-soft s-bad\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><text x=\"24\" y=\"54\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"700\">Unfair</text><text x=\"24\" y=\"83\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"700\">New model</text><text x=\"24\" y=\"100\" font-size=\"13\" class=\"f-muted\">200 tries</text><rect x=\"128\" y=\"72\" width=\"156.7\" height=\"20\" rx=\"3\" class=\"f-indigo\"/><text x=\"290.7\" y=\"87\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\">85.0</text><text x=\"24\" y=\"127\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"700\">Baseline</text><text x=\"24\" y=\"144\" font-size=\"13\" class=\"f-muted\">1 try, default</text><rect x=\"128\" y=\"116\" width=\"62.7\" height=\"20\" rx=\"3\" class=\"f-muted\"/><text x=\"196.7\" y=\"131\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\">82.0</text><text x=\"24\" y=\"172\" font-size=\"14\" class=\"f-bad\" font-weight=\"700\">Gap: +3.0 points</text><text x=\"24\" y=\"192\" font-size=\"13\">Settings were picked by test score,</text><text x=\"24\" y=\"210\" font-size=\"13\">so the test set is no longer unseen.</text><rect x=\"12\" y=\"240\" width=\"336\" height=\"196\" rx=\"10\" class=\"f-ok-soft s-ok\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><text x=\"24\" y=\"262\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"700\">Fair</text><text x=\"24\" y=\"291\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"700\">New model</text><text x=\"24\" y=\"308\" font-size=\"13\" class=\"f-muted\">200 tries</text><rect x=\"128\" y=\"280\" width=\"125.3\" height=\"20\" rx=\"3\" class=\"f-indigo\"/><text x=\"259.3\" y=\"295\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\">84.0</text><text x=\"24\" y=\"335\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"700\">Baseline</text><text x=\"24\" y=\"352\" font-size=\"13\" class=\"f-muted\">200 tries</text><rect x=\"128\" y=\"324\" width=\"112.8\" height=\"20\" rx=\"3\" class=\"f-muted\"/><text x=\"246.8\" y=\"339\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\">83.6</text><text x=\"24\" y=\"380\" font-size=\"14\" class=\"f-ok\" font-weight=\"700\">Gap: +0.4 points</text><text x=\"24\" y=\"400\" font-size=\"13\">Both tuned on a validation set;</text><text x=\"24\" y=\"418\" font-size=\"13\">test set used once, at the end.</text></svg>"
 },
 {
  "id": "gst-four-invoices",
  "after": "commonMistakes",
  "title": "One ₹50,000 project, four invoices.",
  "caption": "Once you are GST-registered, AI and IT services carry 18% GST. For a client in your own state, that is 9% CGST plus 9% SGST; for another state, one 18% IGST (the GST on sales to another state). The client pays ₹59,000 either way. Work for a foreign client usually counts as export, so with a LUT filed you add no IGST. If you are under the turnover limit (₹20 lakh in most states) and not registered, you charge no GST at all. The ₹9,000 is never your income: you pay it to the government with your GST return. Check your own case with a CA.",
  "alt": "Four horizontal bars, each starting with the same 50,000 rupee fee. The first two add 9,000 rupees of GST, as CGST plus SGST for a client in the same state (Pune to Mumbai) or as IGST for another state (Pune to Bengaluru), for a total of 59,000 rupees. The last two, a foreign client under a LUT and a freelancer who is not GST-registered, add nothing and stay at 50,000 rupees.",
  "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 360 339\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><text x=\"16\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"14\"><tspan font-weight=\"700\">Client in your state</tspan><tspan class=\"f-muted\" font-size=\"13\">  Pune → Mumbai</tspan></text><rect x=\"16\" y=\"36\" width=\"200\" height=\"26\" rx=\"4\" class=\"f-indigo-soft s-indigo\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><text x=\"26\" y=\"54\" font-size=\"14\">Fee ₹50,000</text><rect x=\"216\" y=\"36\" width=\"18\" height=\"26\" class=\"f-haldi s-haldi\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><rect x=\"234\" y=\"36\" width=\"18\" height=\"26\" class=\"f-haldi s-haldi\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><line x1=\"234\" y1=\"36\" x2=\"234\" y2=\"62\" class=\"s-ink\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"262\" y=\"54\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"700\">= ₹59,000</text><text x=\"16\" y=\"81\" font-size=\"13\" class=\"f-muted\">+ CGST 9% ₹4,500 + SGST 9% ₹4,500</text><text x=\"16\" y=\"108\" font-size=\"14\"><tspan font-weight=\"700\">Client in another state</tspan><tspan class=\"f-muted\" font-size=\"13\">  Pune → Bengaluru</tspan></text><rect x=\"16\" y=\"118\" width=\"200\" height=\"26\" rx=\"4\" class=\"f-indigo-soft s-indigo\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><text x=\"26\" y=\"136\" font-size=\"14\">Fee ₹50,000</text><rect x=\"216\" y=\"118\" width=\"36\" height=\"26\" class=\"f-haldi s-haldi\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><text x=\"262\" y=\"136\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"700\">= ₹59,000</text><text x=\"16\" y=\"163\" font-size=\"13\" class=\"f-muted\">+ IGST 18% ₹9,000</text><text x=\"16\" y=\"190\" font-size=\"14\"><tspan font-weight=\"700\">Client abroad, LUT filed</tspan><tspan class=\"f-muted\" font-size=\"13\">  export of service</tspan></text><rect x=\"16\" y=\"200\" width=\"200\" height=\"26\" rx=\"4\" class=\"f-indigo-soft s-indigo\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><text x=\"26\" y=\"218\" font-size=\"14\">Fee ₹50,000</text><rect x=\"218\" y=\"201\" width=\"34\" height=\"24\" rx=\"3\" class=\"f-none s-muted\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" stroke-dasharray=\"3 3\"/><text x=\"235\" y=\"218\" font-size=\"13\" class=\"f-muted\" text-anchor=\"middle\">₹0</text><text x=\"262\" y=\"218\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"700\">= ₹50,000</text><text x=\"16\" y=\"245\" font-size=\"13\" class=\"f-muted\">Zero-rated: no IGST to pay</text><text x=\"16\" y=\"272\" font-size=\"14\"><tspan font-weight=\"700\">You are not GST-registered</tspan></text><rect x=\"16\" y=\"282\" width=\"200\" height=\"26\" rx=\"4\" class=\"f-indigo-soft s-indigo\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><text x=\"26\" y=\"300\" font-size=\"14\">Fee ₹50,000</text><rect x=\"218\" y=\"283\" width=\"34\" height=\"24\" rx=\"3\" class=\"f-none s-muted\" stroke-width=\"1.3\" stroke-dasharray=\"3 3\"/><text x=\"235\" y=\"300\" font-size=\"13\" class=\"f-muted\" text-anchor=\"middle\">₹0</text><text x=\"262\" y=\"300\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"700\">= ₹50,000</text><text x=\"16\" y=\"327\" font-size=\"13\" class=\"f-muted\">Turnover under ₹20 lakh a year: no GST</text></svg>"
 },
 {
  "id": "one-page-summary",
  "after": "selfCheck",
  "title": "What a one-page summary looks like.",
  "caption": "Here the template is filled in for \"Attention Is All You Need\", the 2017 paper behind today's chat models. Do the same for the LoRA paper in your own words. Keep each box to one or two lines, and make the limitation (कमी, kami) specific. The same short shape works for your two-minute project pitch.",
  "alt": "A one-page summary card for the 2017 paper Attention Is All You Need. Problem: older translation models read words one by one, so they are slow to train. Key idea: use only attention, so each word looks at all the others at once. Main result: 28.4 BLEU, a translation score, on English to German, a record at the time. One limit: the work grows with the square of the text length. My question: would it work as well for Hindi, with much less data? Below, the two-minute project pitch as four chips joined by arrows: problem, approach, result with a number, next.",
  "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 360 424\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><rect x=\"12\" y=\"10\" width=\"336\" height=\"52\" rx=\"10\" class=\"f-surface2 s-line\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"180\" y=\"31\" font-size=\"15\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"700\">One-page summary, filled in</text><text x=\"180\" y=\"50\" font-size=\"13\" class=\"f-muted\" text-anchor=\"middle\">“Attention Is All You Need” (2017)</text><rect x=\"12\" y=\"72\" width=\"336\" height=\"50\" rx=\"8\" class=\"f-indigo-soft s-indigo\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><text x=\"22\" y=\"93\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\">Problem</text><text x=\"114\" y=\"93\" font-size=\"13\">Older translation models read</text><text x=\"114\" y=\"111\" font-size=\"13\">words one by one: slow to train.</text><rect x=\"12\" y=\"130\" width=\"336\" height=\"50\" rx=\"8\" class=\"f-indigo-soft s-indigo\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><text x=\"22\" y=\"151\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\">Key idea</text><text x=\"114\" y=\"151\" font-size=\"13\">Use only attention: each word</text><text x=\"114\" y=\"169\" font-size=\"13\">looks at all the others at once.</text><rect x=\"12\" y=\"188\" width=\"336\" height=\"50\" rx=\"8\" class=\"f-indigo-soft s-indigo\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><text x=\"22\" y=\"209\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\">Main result</text><text x=\"114\" y=\"209\" font-size=\"13\">28.4 BLEU (a translation score)</text><text x=\"114\" y=\"227\" font-size=\"13\">on English to German: a record.</text><rect x=\"12\" y=\"246\" width=\"336\" height=\"50\" rx=\"8\" class=\"f-haldi-soft s-haldi\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><text x=\"22\" y=\"267\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\">One limit</text><text x=\"114\" y=\"267\" font-size=\"13\">The work grows with the square</text><text x=\"114\" y=\"285\" font-size=\"13\">of the text length.</text><rect x=\"12\" y=\"304\" width=\"336\" height=\"50\" rx=\"8\" class=\"f-ok-soft s-ok\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><text x=\"22\" y=\"325\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\">My question</text><text x=\"114\" y=\"325\" font-size=\"13\">Would it work as well for Hindi,</text><text x=\"114\" y=\"343\" font-size=\"13\">with much less data?</text><text x=\"12\" y=\"376\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"700\">Then the 2-minute project pitch:</text><rect x=\"12\" y=\"388\" width=\"62.9\" height=\"26\" rx=\"13\" class=\"f-surface2 s-line\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"43.4\" y=\"406\" font-size=\"13\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Problem</text><line x1=\"76.9\" y1=\"401\" x2=\"80.9\" y2=\"401\" class=\"s-muted\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><polygon points=\"84.9,401 79.9,403.8 79.9,398.2\" class=\"f-muted\"/><rect x=\"86.9\" y=\"388\" width=\"71.9\" height=\"26\" rx=\"13\" class=\"f-surface2 s-line\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"122.8\" y=\"406\" font-size=\"13\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Approach</text><line x1=\"160.8\" y1=\"401\" x2=\"164.8\" y2=\"401\" class=\"s-muted\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><polygon points=\"168.8,401 163.8,403.8 163.8,398.2\" class=\"f-muted\"/><rect x=\"170.8\" y=\"388\" width=\"113\" height=\"26\" rx=\"13\" class=\"f-surface2 s-line\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"227.3\" y=\"406\" font-size=\"13\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Result + number</text><line x1=\"285.8\" y1=\"401\" x2=\"289.8\" y2=\"401\" class=\"s-muted\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><polygon points=\"293.8,401 288.8,403.8 288.8,398.2\" class=\"f-muted\"/><rect x=\"295.8\" y=\"388\" width=\"40.7\" height=\"26\" rx=\"13\" class=\"f-surface2 s-line\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"316.1\" y=\"406\" font-size=\"13\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Next</text></svg>"
 }
